Core/Core.h: Core.h is U++’s umbrella header, setting build and platform configuration, importing system dependencies, and aggregating core APIs for strings, containers, memory, I/O, networking, parsing, concurrency, and utilities.
Core/config.h: Core/config.h loads user and optional main configuration, detects compiler, operating system, and CPU, and defines platform, architecture, endianness, alignment, and supported C++ standard feature macros.
Core/Defs.h: Defines U++ foundational macros and types: panic/assert and init/exit helpers, fixed-width aliases, move/clone utilities, null sentinels, noncopyable base, heap hooks, and CPU/memory queries.
Core/Ops.h: Core/Ops.h provides low-level numeric and memory utilities: endian swapping and byte-order reads/writes, hash folding, saturation and bit-count operations, plus carry and 64-bit multiplication helpers.
Core/Fn.h: Fn.h defines constexpr variadic min/max, clamp, findarg, and decode helpers, plus tuple-like indexed access and argument-pack utilities to gather values into containers or scatter them into variables. It retains deprecated minmax.
Core/Mem.h: Mem.h provides byte- and typed-element memory utilities for filling, copying, comparing, hashing, and counting values. It uses SIMD-optimized paths when available and portable standard-library or loop-based fallbacks otherwise.
Core/SIMD_SSE2.h: Defines SSE2-backed 128-bit vector types for four floats, four 32-bit ints, eight 16-bit ints, and sixteen 8-bit ints, with arithmetic, comparisons, masks, loads/stores, conversions, broadcasts, and packing helpers.
Core/SIMD_NEON.h: Provides ARM NEON-backed SIMD wrappers for four-lane floats/32-bit integers, eight-lane 16-bit integers, and sixteen-lane bytes. Defines vector arithmetic, comparisons, masks, loads/stores, conversions, packing, and broadcasts.
Core/Atomic.h: Core/Atomic.h provides U++ atomic primitives, including the `Atomic` type and `AtomicInc`/`AtomicDec` helpers, for safely updating shared values across threads.
Core/Mt.h: Defines U++’s cross-platform threading primitives: thread lifecycle and shutdown controls, semaphores, mutexes, reader-writer locks, condition variables, one-time initialization, lazy updates, spinlocks, and optional lock profiling.
Core/Heap.h: Heap.h defines U++ allocation APIs, configurable heap sizing, tiny-block helpers, memory profiling and leak diagnostics. With UPP_HEAP disabled, it provides lightweight malloc/new fallbacks and no-op diagnostics.
Core/HeapImp.h: HeapImp.h defines U++’s internal allocator: block metadata and split/coalesce logic, size-class small allocations, large/huge page management, remote-free buffering, reallocations, and optional heap diagnostics.
Core/String.h: Core/String.h defines UTF-8 `String` and wide `WString`, their mutable buffers and shared string operations: concatenation, search, replacement, trimming, comparison, hashing, conversion, formatting, and character filtering.
Core/CharFilter.h: Defines inline character filters for ASCII/Unicode, digits and numeric input, whitespace, letters, case conversion, and CR/LF. `Filter` removes rejected characters; `FilterWhile` stops at the first rejected character, for narrow and wide strings.
Core/SplitMerge.h: Declares narrow- and wide-string split APIs supporting delimiters, filters, limits, and empty-field control, plus Join and variadic SplitTo/Merge helpers for distributing or combining string values.
Core/CharSet.h: Defines U++ character encoding and Unicode utilities: UTF-8/16/32 conversion, charset registration and conversion, Unicode normalization and character classification/casing, plus BOM-aware stream and file I/O.
Core/Regex.h: Declares PCRE2-backed `Regex` and `WRegex` for UTF-8 and wide-character patterns, with configurable compilation, matching against strings or buffers, error reporting, and `RegexMatch` capture offsets, lengths, and extraction.
Core/Path.h: Declares cross-platform path and filename utilities, normalization, file/directory operations and timestamps, symlink and temporary-path helpers, file enumeration, filesystem metadata, and Windows network-node discovery.
Core/App.h: Core/App.h declares application-level helpers for environment, executable and user paths, configuration, command-line access, startup/shutdown and exit codes, data files, browser launch, system folders, admin checks, and crash hooks.
Core/Huge.h: `Huge` stores large byte sequences in an array of 1 MiB blocks. It supports appending chunks, marking the final chunk’s size, querying total size, and retrieving data by range or as a `String`.
Core/Stream.h: Defines U++ stream abstractions for memory, strings, files, blocks, comparison, and output, with stream errors and file modes. Provides helpers for loading, saving, copying, packing, and standard console I/O.
Core/FilterStream.h: Defines input and output filter-stream adapters that connect a stream to a filter’s `Put`/`End` callbacks. They buffer data, handle EOF and flushing, and expose output byte counts and position events.
Core/FileMapping.h: FileMapping provides cross-platform file mapping: open or create files, map whole files or byte ranges into memory, access mapped bytes through pointers and indexing, and unmap or close the resource.
Core/Profile.h: Core/Profile.h provides lightweight profiling helpers: `TimingInspector` records call counts, elapsed-time totals and extrema with nesting via an RAII routine; `HitCountInspector` tracks hits. Macros simplify timing and hit counting.
Core/Diag.h: Core/Diag.h defines exceptions, configurable logging streams and formats, hex dumps, debug-only assertions/timing macros, container/map diagnostics, crash-dump hooks, log-etalon checks, and type-name/demangling helpers.
Core/Util.h: Util.h declares Core utilities for timing, INI configuration, charset and text handling, hex/base64 encoding, randomness and math, error reporting, multipart streams, serialization/config persistence, string replacement, and spelling support.
Core/LocalProcess.h: Defines an abstract process interface and cross-platform `LocalProcess` for launching commands, exchanging stdin/stdout/stderr, checking or killing processes, and retrieving exit status. Includes charset controls and `Sys` helpers.
Core/BinUndoRedo.h: Please provide the contents of `Core/BinUndoRedo.h` so I can summarize it accurately.
Core/Topt.h: Core/Topt.h provides foundational template utilities for U++: comparison and arithmetic operators, type traits for copy/move/relocation, iterator helpers, and hash/equality support for values and containers.
Core/Range.h: Core/Range.h provides generic range adapters and type aliases for values and iterators. It supports subranges, repeated-value ranges, reversed and indexed views, plus filtered or sorted views, with iteration and range comparison.
Core/Algo.h: Core/Algo.h provides generic range algorithms: numeric helpers, reversal, accumulation and sums, counting, min/max selection, range comparison, predicate/value searches, binary bounds and lookup, LRU updates, iota generation, and random shuffling.
Core/CoAlgo.h: Provides parallel range algorithms built on CoWork partitioning: reductions and sums, counts, min/max searches, matching/index lookup, range equality, and collecting all matches, with serial fallback for small inputs.
Core/Sorted.h: Provides in-place algorithms for sorted containers: append-merge, set union, removal, and intersection. Each supports a custom ordering predicate, with overloads defaulting to `std::less` for the container’s value type.
Core/CoSort.h: CoSort.h provides parallel sorting algorithms using CoWork, including unstable and stable sorts, index-based sorting of multiple ranges, sort-order generation, and helpers to sort map keys, values, or indexes.
Core/Obsolete.h: Obsolete.h provides deprecated compatibility helpers for comparisons, field/method-based relations, appending and searching containers, equality checks, sums, and binary-search bounds. Its declarations are enabled only when `DEPRECATED` is defined.
Core/Sort.h: Core/Sort.h provides generic sorting utilities for ranges and containers, including standard and stable sorts, index/order generation, and sorting by keys or values. It also defines iterator adapters used by these algorithms.
Core/Vcont.h: Core/Vcont.h declares U++’s fundamental dynamic containers: Buffer, Vector, Array, Index, and helpers for creation, insertion, removal, range operations, comparison, and iterator support.
Core/BiCont.h: Core/BiCont.h defines BiVector and BiArray, bidirectional sequence containers supporting efficient insertion and removal at both ends, with iterator access, comparisons, and array/vector-style value storage.
Core/Other.h: Defines miscellaneous Core utilities: a move-only type-erased `Any`, dynamic bit storage, keyed packed data, intrusive list links, and a templated LRU cache with sizing, eviction, and removal operations.
Core/Index.h: `Index<T>` is a moveable, deep-copyable key collection backed by a vector and hash table. It supports fast lookup and insertion, duplicate keys, unlinking/sweeping entries, capacity management, serialization, and iteration.
Core/Map.h: Defines U++ ordered key-value map templates: `AMap` combines an `Index` with value storage for lookup, insertion, removal, iteration, and serialization; `VectorMap` and `ArrayMap` provide vector- and pointer-array-backed variants.
Core/FixedMap.h: Defines fixed-key maps that accumulate key/value pairs, then sort them for binary-search lookup. Provides indexed and iterator access, duplicate-key traversal, and Vector- or Array-backed variants with serialization support.
Core/InVector.h: Defines block-based `InVector` and owning `InArray` containers with STL-style iterators, indexed insertion/removal, and binary-search helpers, plus sorted indexes and vector-/array-backed sorted maps.
Core/Tuple.h: Defines U++ tuples of up to four elements, with indexed/type-based access, comparison, hashing, serialization, Value conversion, and C++17 structured-binding support. Includes MakeTuple, FindTuple, and reference-binding Tie helpers.
Core/Function.h: `Function.h` defines a type-erased, reference-counted callable with copy/move support, invocation, clearing, and chained callbacks. It also provides `Event`/`Gate` aliases and `MemFn` helpers for binding member functions.
Core/Callback.h: Provides backward-compatible `CallbackN` and `GateN` wrappers over `Function` for void and bool callbacks, with proxying, binding macros, arity aliases, and a callback-backed target for assigning values.
Core/TimeDate.h: Defines U++ Date and Time types with validity, comparison, arithmetic, serialization, calendar and week calculations, localized names, parsing/formatting, system-clock access, and file-time, timezone, and UTC conversions.
Core/Value.h: Defines U++’s dynamically typed `Value`, with built-in and registered custom types, conversions, comparison, serialization, XML/JSON support, array/map access, and helpers for null, error, numeric, and date-time values.
Core/ValueUtil.h: ValueUtil.h adds null-default helpers and Value comparison/order strategies, plus lightweight IDs and typed references. It defines dynamic ValueArray/ValueMap containers with lookup, mutation, comparison, serialization, and a ValueGen interface.
Core/Complex.h: `Complex` wraps `std::complex<double>` for U++: it supports `Value` and `Ref` conversion, null handling, hashing, string formatting, serialization/XML/JSON, and helpers for magnitude, NaN, infinity, finiteness, and comparisons.
Core/Format.h: Core/Format.h declares integer, floating-point, date and time formatting, with precision and notation flags; it also provides localized argument formatting, formatter registration, Sprintf/DeFormat, and numeric AsString overloads.
Core/Convert.h: Core/Convert.h declares numeric and date/time string parsing/formatting helpers, plus a polymorphic Value converter interface. Specialized converters support bounds, null handling, filtering, trimming, mapping, composition, and lambda-defined behavior.
Core/Color.h: Defines RGBA pixels and the `Color` value type, including null/special and theme-aware colors. Provides named colors, RGB/HSV/CMYK conversion, blending, luminance and contrast calculations, and HTML text conversion.
Core/Gtypes.h: Defines templated 2D sizes, points, and rectangles with arithmetic, geometry, containment, scaling, and serialization helpers. Provides common integer, 16-bit, 64-bit, and floating-point aliases plus alignment and fit-size utilities.
Core/i18n.h: Provides U++ internationalization APIs: register translation modules, look up localized strings, inspect and save/load language catalogs, and set the active language. Defines `t_` for translation and `tt_` for unchanged text.
Core/t.h: Defines locale-specific translation macros and `T_`, assigns language-version counters, and builds a translation table from `TFILE` during initialization, registering it as a language module before cleaning up the macros.
Core/Lang.h: Defines U++ language IDs and localization APIs for selecting languages, retrieving translated text and locale metadata, and configuring charsets. `LanguageInfo` provides localized formatting, names, and text comparison; module records register translations.
Core/Parser.h: Core/Parser.h declares `CParser`, a C/C++-style text parser with position and error tracking, plus helpers for recognizing identifier characters and escaping strings as C string literals.
Core/XML.h: Core/XML.h declares XML escaping and markup helpers, a configurable stream parser with tag, attribute, text, and entity access, an editable XmlNode tree, filtered parsing APIs, and options for serializing documents to strings, streams, or files.
Core/Xmlize.h: Xmlize.h provides XML serialization support: attribute load/store helpers, Xmlize overloads and container/map adapters, and APIs for serializing to or loading from XML strings, files, and JSON-compatible values.
Core/JSON.h: Core/JSON.h provides JSON parsing and encoding, object/array builders, and JsonIO for templated serialization of values, containers, and maps. It also offers value/string/file load-store helpers and JSON Pointer lookup.
Core/Uuid.h: `Uuid` defines a 128-bit identifier with null handling, equality and hashing, serialization to streams/XML/JSON and `Value`, plus creation (including v4), formatting, and scanning utilities.
Core/Ptr.h: Core/Ptr.h defines U++’s `Ptr<T>` non-owning observer pointer and the `Pte`/`PteBase` machinery that lets tracked objects notify pointers when they are destroyed, preventing dangling references.
Core/z.h: Defines CRC-32 utilities and configurable zlib/gzip compression and decompression for streams, strings, buffers, and files. Includes filter-stream wrappers, progress callbacks, checksum/header options, and fast compression helpers.
Core/Topic.h: Defines movable `Topic` records and `TopicLink` references, with helpers to format and parse links, retrieve topics by package/group/name or path (including localized lookup), and access the topic database.
Core/topic_group.h: This header assigns unique initialization-block IDs to included topic files, defines macros for topic ID, title, compressed byte data, and registration, then includes TOPICFILE to register its topic at startup.
Core/CoWork.h: Please provide the contents of `Core/CoWork.h` so I can summarize it.
Core/ValueCache.h: Defines U++ value-cache APIs around LRUCache: create or retrieve cached Values by generated keys, manage global cache sizing and eviction under a mutex, and provide main-thread and thread-local caching.
Core/Hash.h: Core/Hash.h declares streaming and one-shot MD5, SHA-1, SHA-256, xxHash, and xxHash64 APIs. Hash streams accept data through OutStream and provide reset, final digest, and byte- or String-based results.
Core/Inet.h: Core/Inet.h declares networking utilities for URL/HTML and Base64 encoding, MIME and HMAC helpers, async DNS, TCP/SSL sockets, URL and HTTP parsing/client requests, cookies, proxy handling, and WebSocket communication.
Core/dli.h: Core/dli.h is a macro-driven template for dynamic-library wrappers. It generates function/data pointer declarations from a DLI header and provides lazy loading, required-load checks, library naming, and cleanup.
Core/Win32Util.h: Please provide the contents of `Core/Win32Util.h` so I can summarize it.
